# Identity and TAK presence

WinTAKTracker is tracking-only. Map clients (CloudTAK / ATAK / WinTAK) show PLI from CoT. TAK Server and Portal connection lists identify a TLS session from the **first usable self-SA (PLI)**.

## Callsign sources

1. **Per-user callsign** (`userIdentities[sid]`) — when an interactive tray session is bound; this is what operators set under Identity → “My callsign”.
2. **Sticky last user** (default after logoff) — `lastInteractiveUserSid` keeps that user’s callsign while the service runs headless. Opt into computer fallback with Identity → “On logoff, use computer callsign” (`revertToComputerCallsignOnLogoff`).
3. **Computer callsign** (`computerIdentity`) — bootstrap before any user callsign exists, and when computer-on-logoff is enabled. Default = Windows computer name.
4. Never put a **bare hostname** in CoT `remarks` (some Portal UIs mis-read that as the callsign). Optional remarks must be prefixed (`Computer: {name}`). Default `IncludeComputerNameInRemarks` is **off**.

## Presence announce (must keep working)

- After TAK connect: delay briefly, then `AnnouncePresenceAsync` so tray `SetActiveSession` can win the race before the first PLI.
- When active session / callsign changes: re-announce so Portal/Server labels update from machine name → user callsign.
- Self-SA must include ATAK-shaped fields: `contact@callsign` + `endpoint=*:-1:stcp`, `uid@Droid` (= callsign), `__group`, `takv platform=WinTAKTracker`, `precisionlocation`.
- Reply to server `t-x-c-t` with `t-x-c-t-r`.
- Device UID: `WINDOWS-WinTAKTracker-*` for new installs (existing `WIN-*` OK). Do **not** spoof `ANDROID-*` or `ATAK-CIV`.

## Client certs (Windows Schannel)

Load client `.p12` with `MachineKeySet` (service) / `UserKeySet` (portable) via `SchannelCertificateLoader`. Never use `EphemeralKeySet` for SslStream mTLS on Windows.

## Portal vs map

- CloudTAK/ATAK maps use `contact@callsign` — that is the source of truth for “am I tracking?”
- Portal Connected Users may omit raw SSL clients or lag on first-PLI identity; that is often Portal-side. See `docs/managed-devices.md`.

## Secrets

Follow `no-tak-secrets.mdc`. No real hosts, tokens, enroll URLs, or certs in the repo.
